From: Warder Evolution <noreply@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] enigma2: fetch service event independently of EPG text font for native progressbar

The native progressbar painter relies on evt being populated by the
celServiceInfo text branch. Setting that font to null skips the branch,
so native left/right progressbars disappear even though their geometry
and pixmaps remain configured. Fetch the event specifically for progress
painting if needed. No synthetic bars, no image overlay, and no
changes to percentage/minute text modes.

--- a/lib/service/listboxservice.cpp
+++ b/lib/service/listboxservice.cpp
@@
 		eRect area = m_element_position[celServiceEventProgressbar];
+		// A progressbar is independent of the optional EPG-description font.
+		// If celServiceInfo was disabled, evt has not been fetched by the
+		// text-painting loop. Obtain it here for the native progressbar.
+		if (area.width() > 0 && !evt && !m_element_font[celServiceEventProgressbar]
+			&& isPlayable && service_info)
+			service_info->getEvent(*m_cursor, evt);
 		if (area.width() > 0 && evt && !m_element_font[celServiceEventProgressbar])
 		{
